WEBVTT

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.120
MAN: Well, good night.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.040
ANDY'S MOM: Goodbye.
Drive safe.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.520
(GRUNTS)

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.960
ANDY: Oh, there you are.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.000
Mom, I found him! I found him!

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.840
ANDY'S MOM: Oh, good.
Come on and get inside.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.640
(YOU'VE GOT A FRIEND IN ME
PLAYING)

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.880
MAN: (SINGING)
You've got a friend in me

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.120
VOICE BOX: Reach for the sky!

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.800
MAN: (SINGING)
You've got a friend in me

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.280
Ride 'em, cowboy! Yee-haw!

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.040
When the road looks
rough ahead

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.800
VOICE BOX:
There's a snake in my boot.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.720
And you're miles and miles
From your nice warm bed

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.800
(ANDY LAUGHING)

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.000
You just remember
what your old pal said

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.160
Boy, you've got a friend in me

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.680
To infinity and beyond!

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.640
Yeah, you've got
a friend in me

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.600
(GASPS) My cowboy!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.320
Now, some other folks might be
a little bit smarter than I am

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.680
Big and stronger, too

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.360
-Woody, let's go!
-(ANDY CHUCKLES)

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.520
Maybe

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.680
But none of them will ever
love you the way I do

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.040
VOICE BOX:
You're my favorite deputy!

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.760
It's me and you, boy

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.280
And as the years go by

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.520
Our friendship will never die

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.520
Reach for the sky!

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.360
You're gonna see
it's our destiny

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.960
They've escaped and they're
headed right for us!

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.320
-(YELLS, GIGGLES)
-You've got a friend in me

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.760
-Full speed ahead! Yay!
-You've got a friend in me

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.720
You've got a friend in me

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:27.960
TRIXIE:
It's getting hot in here!

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.040
MR. POTATO HEAD:
Where's my ear?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.120
HAMM: You're on my foot!

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.200
BUTTERCUP: Oh, hey,
quit shoving.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.280
TRIXIE: Sorry!
SLINKY: Could you move over

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.600
-a bit, please?
-TRIXIE: That was my horn.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.960
(TOY SHUSHING)

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.160
BUZZ'S VOICE BOX:
To infinity and beyond!

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.280
BUZZ: I know that was you,
Potato Head.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.360
(MR. POTATO HEAD LAUGHING)

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.200
Everyone, listen.
I thought I told you...

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.280
when Mom quickly cleans
the bedroom like that...

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.080
expect to be put
in the closet.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.920
(WHIMPERS) How much longer?

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.440
Keep it to a dull roar, Rex.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.200
Deep breaths, Jessie.
Deep breaths.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:50.720
-(JESSIE HYPERVENTILATING)
-Settle down, Slink.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.000
Sit. Good boy!

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.280
Sheriff,
do I need to be worried?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.200
No, no. My guys are veterans.
They'll hang in there.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.360
Good. Just keep them calm
until we get word.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.520
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.640
How are you, uh,
feeling about today?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.120
Uh, good, good. Yeah, good.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.360
I'm good.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.000
Uh... Good.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.200
(TINKLING)

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.120
We're on!
Bonnie's done with breakfast!

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.640
-Any minute now.
-You hear that?

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.920
Any minute now.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.080
Wind 'em if you got 'em.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.120
Keep your batteries clean,
your joints unlocked...

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.280
Uh, thanks, Woody.
I got it.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.640
Yes, I'm sorry.
You're right, you're right.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.760
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.280
The town is open!

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.440
Hi, Mayor!

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.520
Banker!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.160
Hi, Ice-Cream Man!
Hi, Hat Shop Owner!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.680
Mailman!

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.360
And the sheriff!

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.000
Okay. Bye, toys!

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.960
Yee-haw! Sheriff Jessie!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.800
Giddy-up, Bullseye!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.880
(BONNIE IMITATES
HORSE GALLOPING)

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.040
They went that way!

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.320
Chase them!

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.920
(CLEARS THROAT, GRUNTS)

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.160
What a beautiful hat shop!
You have so many hats...

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.840
MELEPHANT BROOKS: Wow.
They're doing "hat shop."

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.080
CARL REINEROCEROS:
When's the last time

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.200
we ever got to play that?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.760
Remember when
she played "house"?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:00.840
I liked "house."

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.120
Those were the days.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.680
It was basic.
You made a house,

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.760
you lived in it, done.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.520
Hmm. That's the third time

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.840
you haven't been picked
this week.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.280
I don't know.
I don't keep count.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.080
Oh, you don't have to.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.040
-I'll do it for you.
-Okay, okay, okay, I get it.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.240
It's been a while.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.840
Oh, looky there.
You got your first dust bunny.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.000
CHAIROL BURNETT:
Aw, how adorable.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.240
What you gonna name it?

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Uh, what about Dusty?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.560
MELEPHANT BROOKS: Francis!
CHAIROL BURNETT: Harry!

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.680
CARL REINEROCEROS: Karen!
MELEPHANT BROOKS: Fuzzball!

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.840
-LeBron?
-No, Fluffy.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.440
-How about Thumper?
-CHAIROL BURNETT: Tumbleweed!

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.200
"Tumbleweed."
Oh, that's good. That's good.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.280
MELEPHANT BROOKS:
He's a cowboy,

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.440
-so that makes a lot of sense.
-(SIGHS)

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.240
So many choices.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.600
I just can't decide!

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.720
BONNIE'S DAD: Bonnie?

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.040
What are you doing?
We gotta go.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.120
You don't wanna be late

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.400
for kindergarten orientation,
do you?

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.720
But I don't wanna go.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.200
BONNIE'S DAD: (CHUCKLES)
We talked about this.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.520
We're gonna meet
your teachers,

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.440
-see your classroom...
-Can I bring a toy?

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.400
Toys don't go to school,
that's the rule.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.560
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.760
Freeze! Nobody move!

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.120
Bonnie always
forgets something.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.560
She'll be back any second.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:57.920
That goes for you, too, Hamm.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.080
But it's money!

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.960
You all right, Woody?

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.160
I'm sure she'll pick you
next time.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.240
Oh, come on, I'm fine.
No problem.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.480
Hey, Woody. Here.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.640
Oh, thanks, Jessie.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.440
We're here for you, buddy.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.200
I don't want to play
the baker.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.280
Pricklepants.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.400
The hat shop owner is
the role I was born to play!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.040
All right, Pricklepants,
back to your bakery.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.120
Excuse me, Dolly?

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.560
Woody, can't you see
I'm threatening everyone?

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.640
Go back to the closet.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:19.760
Yeah, I know, I know.
It's just...

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.000
I'm worried about Bonnie.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.880
A toy should go with her
to orientation.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.000
Didn't you hear Dad?
You'll get Bonnie in trouble.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.840
Yeah, but kindergarten
is so different.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.560
It can be too much for a kid.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.880
Having a buddy with them
to get through it

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:30.960
can really help things.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.680
I remember with Andy, I would
go to school with him...

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.800
Uh-huh. I'm sorry, Woody,

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.000
I hate to sound
like a broken record...

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.480
but Bonnie's not Andy.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.000
No, no, no, of course,
I get that.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.320
But if you would just...

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.920
Places, everyone!

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.360
(SIGHS)

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.160
-(DOOR OPENS)
-(FOOTSTEPS RUNNING)

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:46.680
(BONNIE CRYING)

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.880
BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.160
What are you doing back there?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.400
Come on, we have to go.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.200
-That's my big girl.
-(BONNIE SNIFFLES)

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.800
Come on. We gotta hurry, okay?

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.600
Don't forget your backpack.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.320
BONNIE'S MOM: You're gonna
have so much fun.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.880
All right. Now what was it
you were saying, Woody?

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.400
Woody?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.400
BONNIE'S MOM: Here we are.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.960
(CHILDREN CHATTERING
AND LAUGHING)

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.160
BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie, honey,
it'll be okay.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.400
WENDY: Hi! Are you Bonnie?

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:50.720
My name is Miss Wendy.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.280
I'm going to be
your kindergarten teacher.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.440
We have a special place where
you can put your backpack.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.440
You want to see?

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.760
(GIRLS CHATTERING)

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.320
WENDY: Here we are, Bonnie.
Just for you.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.920
Okay, class, let's all find
a seat at a table...

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.280
so we can start craft time.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.720
On the first day of school,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.840
you'll need a place
to put your pencils.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.200
So, today, we're going
to make pencil holders.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:35.680
Now, everyone take a cup...

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.920
and we'll use the art supplies
to decorate them.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.600
Hi.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.520
(GASPS)

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.640
(WHIMPERS SOFTLY)

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:50.880
(SPITS)

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.000
(WOODY GROANS)

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.920
(CHILDREN LAUGHING)

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:06.800
(GRUNTS)

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.640
(SNIFFLING)

